    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557">

                <pb facs="0679" n="669" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg669"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12–2048</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Koo</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi><anchor n="54" xml:id="d557-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1949-01-06">January 6, 1949</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>The Chinese Ambassador presents his compliments to the Secretary of State and has
                    the honor to request that the Secretary be good enough to transmit to the
                    President of the United States the accompanying message, which is addressed to
                    the President by the Members of the National Assembly of the Republic of China.
                    This Assembly, which is composed of over one thousand and six hundred
                    representatives of the people, was responsible for the adoption of the
                    Constitution on December 25, 1946, and the election of the President and Vice
                    President of China. Pursuant to the Constitution it still exercises certain
                    political powers on behalf of the whole body of citizens.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>, December 20, 1948.</p>


                <xi:include href="d557-a1.xml" xpointer="d557-a1"/>
            </div>
